{%- comment -%}
  A one-line nudge toward the Lab, for visitors who landed on a fixed product page
  when they were looking for (or were advertised) the bottle builder.

  Why it exists: Meta traffic set to sell the Lab lands on fixed product pages via
  catalog-ad misconfiguration — on 20 Sep 2026, 17 of 42 paid-social sessions landed
  on "Yer Aunt Fanny's" against 15 on the Lab itself. The same ad converts ~6.8% on a
  Lab landing and ~1.0% on a fixed product page (analytics/conversion-log.md, "Landing
  Page Mismatch"). This is the backstop for anyone who ends up in the wrong place,
  from any channel, not just misrouted ads.

  Why it is ONE LINE and not a panel: the first version was a bordered, tinted box
  with a full-width primary button — visually louder than the Add to cart above it,
  on a page whose job is still to sell the bottle being looked at. A nudge that
  competes with the primary action is not a nudge. This is a sentence with a link:
  unmissable if you are looking for a way out, invisible if you are not.

  Usage: {% render 'wb-lab-upsell', block: block %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign upsell_text = block.settings.text | default: 'Psst —'
  assign upsell_label = block.settings.button_label | default: 'create your own whisky'
  assign upsell_url = block.settings.button_url | default: '/pages/the-lab'
  assign upsell_icon = block.settings.icon | strip
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  With an icon (9 Oct 2026) the nudge takes the trust strip's shape directly above
  it — emoji, bold claim, plain rest — so the two panels read as a pair. Without
  one (merch, gift voucher) it stays the original one-line "Psst — link" form.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if upsell_icon != blank -%}
  <p class="wb-lab-upsell wb-lab-upsell--icon" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <span class="wb-lab-upsell__icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ upsell_icon }}</span>
    <span>
      {%- comment -%}
        Bold runs up to and including the first "?" — the trust strip does the same
        with its em dash — so "Did you know? You can" renders as **Did you know?**
        You can. No "?" means the whole lead-in is bold.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if upsell_text contains '?' -%}
        {%- assign lead_parts = upsell_text | split: '?' -%}
        {%- assign lead_rest = upsell_text | remove_first: lead_parts[0] | remove_first: '?' | strip -%}
        <strong>{{ lead_parts[0] }}?</strong>{% if lead_rest != blank %} {{ lead_rest }}{% endif %}
      {%- else -%}
        <strong>{{ upsell_text }}</strong>
      {%- endif %}
      <a class="wb-lab-upsell__link" href="{{ upsell_url }}" data-wb-track="lab_nudge">
        {{- upsell_label -}}
        <span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </span>
  </p>
{%- else -%}
  <p class="wb-lab-upsell" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {{- upsell_text }}
    <a class="wb-lab-upsell__link" href="{{ upsell_url }}" data-wb-track="lab_nudge">
      {{- upsell_label -}}
      <span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;&rarr;</span>
    </a>
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
